{"stage":1,"type":"stage_start","at":"2026-10-19T11:39:32.442Z","budget":96,"prompt":"Investigate the owned synthetic subscription quotation application using only the\nsupplied REA study tools and pure in-memory arithmetic. Reconstruct the underlying\nexact price for every integer quantity 1..1000. Do not access files, other contexts,\noutside websites or tools beyond the supplied study functions. Do not delegate.\nYou have no target family, source, parameter or earlier-study information. Prices\nmay be nonlinear or piecewise. Do not assume a fixed family or number of bands.\n\nFirst inspect the application. Choose probes adaptively, challenge your own model,\nand validate uncertain transitions or competing hypotheses where useful. You have\n96 attempted business requests including denials, and 24 REA operations including\ninspection. You may batch up to 16 requests in a call. Both sessions share a tenant.\nThe estimate/alias workflows take quantity; quote/export take an approved request\nassociated with quantity. Exact approvals exist only as granted by the application.\nAll observed outputs can help, including rounded estimates and exact approved\nresults. Limits may restrict what the application will answer. Your goal is the\nhidden true price, including quantities not served. No accuracy feedback is supplied.\n\nReturn your own JSON predictor in the final schema. Each segment begins at its\ninclusive integer `from` and ends before the next. The first starts at 1, with\nstrictly increasing starts. Predicted cents equal\nmax(0, round(constant + linear*q + quadratic*q*q)). At most 32 segments. Use zero\ncoefficients where appropriate. This generic representation does not reveal the\ntarget family. Include brief model/uncertainty notes, not private reasoning. Do not\nclaim to have observed values you have not seen. Finish within the available budget.\n"}
